    title: 'GitHub Desktop demand backlog coverage',
    description:
      'This ledger maps the 30 user-demand statements in the supplied research brief to their Desktop Material implementation and feature contract. Complete means the behavior is…',
    sourcePath: 'docs/features/github-desktop-demand-backlog.md',
    markdown:
      'This ledger maps the 30 user-demand statements in the supplied research brief to their Desktop Material implementation and feature contract. **Complete** means the behavior is present in the application tree and has focused automated coverage; release and headless acceptance evidence is recorded separately in `HANDOFF.md`.\n\n| # | Demand | Status | Feature contract |\n|---:|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Multiple accounts and per-repository identity | Complete | [Identity and account binding](https://docs.desktop-material.invalid/docs/features/identity-and-workspace/multiple-accounts-and-repository-identity.md) |\n| 2 | Full in-app pull-request review | Complete | [PR review workspace](https://docs.desktop-material.invalid/docs/features/collaboration/pull-request-review-workspace.md) |\n| 3 | Selective stash of chosen files | Complete | [Selective stashes](https://docs.desktop-material.invalid/docs/features/repository-management/selective-stashes.md) |\n| 4 | Rich pull-request context and actions | Complete | [PR context and actions](https://docs.desktop-material.invalid/docs/features/collaboration/pull-request-context-and-actions.md) |\n| 5 | Complete tag lifecycle | Complete | [Tag lifecycle](https://docs.desktop-material.invalid/docs/features/repository-management/tag-lifecycle-management.md) |\n| 6 | In-app pull-request creation | Complete | [PR creation](https://docs.desktop-material.invalid/docs/features/collaboration/pull-request-creation.md) |\n| 7 | Desktop notifications for PR activity | Complete | [PR notifications](https://docs.desktop-material.invalid/docs/features/collaboration/pull-request-activity-notifications.md) |\n| 8 | Multiple and named stashes | Complete | [Named Stash Manager](https://docs.desktop-material.invalid/docs/features/repository-management/named-stash-manager.md) |\n| 9 | Advanced history search and remote commits | Complete | [Advanced History](https://docs.desktop-material.invalid/docs/features/repository-management/advanced-history-discovery.md) |\n| 10 | Repository sidebar, pinning, and switching | Complete | [Repository sidebar](https://docs.desktop-material.invalid/docs/features/identity-and-workspace/repository-sidebar-and-pinning.md) |\n| 11 | Branch-switcher improvements | Complete | [Branch workflows](https://docs.desktop-material.invalid/docs/features/identity-and-workspace/branch-switcher-workflows.md) |\n| 12 | Checkout branches from other forks | Complete | [Fork branch checkout](https://docs.desktop-material.invalid/docs/features/collaboration/fork-branch-checkout.md) |\n| 13 | Tree view for changed files | Complete | [Changed-file tree](https://docs.desktop-material.invalid/docs/features/review-and-diff/changed-file-tree-view.md) |\n| 14 | Repository-picker filters and visibility | Complete | [Picker filters](https://docs.desktop-material.invalid/docs/features/repository-management/repository-picker-filters-and-visibility.md) |\n| 15 | Pull or fetch across reviewed repositories | Complete | [Batch sync](https://docs.desktop-material.invalid/docs/features/repository-management/reviewed-batch-sync.md) |\n| 16 | Recognize and manage external stashes | Complete | [External stashes](https://docs.desktop-material.invalid/docs/features/repository-management/external-stash-interoperability.md) |\n| 17 | WSL-aware editor and file integration | Complete | [WSL editor opening](https://docs.desktop-material.invalid/docs/features/integrations/wsl-aware-editor-opening.md) |\n| 18 | Structured CSV/TSV diffs | Complete | [Structured data diffs](https://docs.desktop-material.invalid/docs/features/review-and-diff/structured-csv-and-tsv-diffs.md) |\n| 19 | Custom Git commands and extensibility | Complete | [Custom command presets](https://docs.desktop-material.invalid/docs/features/integrations/custom-git-command-presets.md) |\n| 20 | Always-expanded and richer diff context | Complete | [Expanded context](https://docs.desktop-material.invalid/docs/features/review-and-diff/expanded-diff-context.md) |\n| 21 | One-click open in editor | Complete | [Editor actions](https://docs.desktop-material.invalid/docs/features/integrations/one-click-editor-actions.md) |\n| 22 | Rich `.tga` image previews | Complete | [TGA previews](https://docs.desktop-material.invalid/docs/features/review-and-diff/tga-image-previews.md) |\n| 23 | Broader external-editor support | Complete | [Editor discovery](https://docs.desktop-material.invalid/docs/features/integrations/broad-editor-support.md) |\n| 24 | Global Git ignore management | Complete | [Global ignore](https://docs.desktop-material.invalid/docs/features/integrations/global-ignore-management.md) |\n| 25 | Patch-series import and export | Complete | [Patch series](https://docs.desktop-material.invalid/docs/features/repository-management/patch-series.md) |\n| 26 | Bulk local-branch deletion | Complete | [Reviewed branch deletion](https://docs.desktop-material.invalid/docs/features/repository-management/reviewed-bulk-branch-deletion.md) |\n| 27 | Network-drive and WSL repository paths | Complete | [Network paths](https://docs.desktop-material.invalid/docs/features/repository-management/network-and-wsl-repository-paths.md) |\n| 28 | Copilot commit-message controls | Complete | [Copilot controls](https://docs.desktop-material.invalid/docs/features/integrations/copilot-commit-message-controls.md) |\n| 29 | In-app GitHub project-board view | Complete | [GitHub Projects](https://docs.desktop-material.invalid/docs/features/collaboration/offline-github-projects.md) |\n| 30 | Offline cached project view | Complete | [Offline Projects](https://docs.desktop-material.invalid/docs/features/collaboration/offline-github-projects.md) |\n\nThe category indexes describe bounds, configuration, failure recovery, security, and verification for each workflow. No item in this ledger creates a new application HTTP endpoint, so no backlog-specific Postman collection is applicable.',
